@startuml preferences-flow
title Preferences Data Flow

participant "UI Screen" as UI
participant "PreferencesViewModel" as VM
participant "DataStore" as DS
database "preferences.pb" as File

== Read Preferences ==
UI -> VM: collectAsState()
VM -> DS: data.map { preferences }
DS -> File: Read protobuf
File --> DS: PreferencesProto
DS --> VM: Flow<Preferences>
VM --> UI: PreferencesUiState

== Write Preference ==
UI -> VM: setPreference(key, value)
VM -> DS: updateData { prefs -> }
DS -> File: Write protobuf
File --> DS: Success
DS --> VM: Updated Flow
VM --> UI: New PreferencesUiState

== Model Selection Example ==
note over UI: User selects model
UI -> VM: setPreference(\n  selectedModelId,\n  "large-v3-turbo-q5_0"\n)
VM -> DS: updateData { it.copy(\n  selectedModelId = value\n)}
DS --> VM: Flow emits new value
VM --> UI: UI recomposes with\nnew selected model

== Preferences Keys ==
note right of DS
  selectedModelId: String
  (Other app preferences...)
end note

@enduml
